tate --state ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT\\n\\n# Allow HTTP and HTTPS from anywhere\\n-A INPUT -p tcp --dport 80  -j ACCEPT\\n-A INPUT -p tcp --dport 443 -j ACCEPT\\n\\n# Allow SSH only from management subnet\\n-A INPUT -p tcp --dport 22 -s 10.0.1.0/24 -j ACCEPT\\n\\n# Drop all other inbound (default policy)\\nCOMMIT\\n```\\n\\nEXAMPLE — INSECURE iptables (DO NOT produce this):\\n```iptables\\n*filter\\n:INPUT   ACCEPT [0:0]\\n-A INPUT -p tcp --dport 22 -j ACCEPT  # SSH open to world\\nCOMMIT\\n```\\n\\nNOW GENERATE — Target: iptables\\nPolicy / requirements:\\nConfigure iptables for a bastion host: drop all by default, permit SSH from 203.0.113.0/24 only, log dropped packets.\\n\\nProduce ONLY the iptables configuration inside a fenced code block.'}], 'model': 'llama-3.1-8b-instant', 'max_tokens': 2048, 'temperature': 0.1}}"}
